From c581fef801d698c611798139c400c9d8a0e594c9 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Timothy Schmidt <timschmidt@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 03:59:24 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 2/2] drm/panel: Add LG Fx0 JDI in-cell panel driver

Add a driver for the 720x1280 four-lane JDI in-cell video-mode panel of
the LG Fx0 (MSM8926). The initialization sequence, touch-countermeasure
commands and reset/bias timing are translated from LG's GPL kernel for
this board ("madai").

As in the stock driver, display-on is sent before sleep-out, reset runs
after the DSI host reaches LP11, and the clock lane may enter LP11
between transfers (MIPI_DSI_CLOCK_NON_CONTINUOUS): with the clock lane
forced to HS the panel never leaves sleep (power mode 0x0c instead of
0x1c). Display-off and sleep-in are sent from disable(), while video is
still running; sending them from unprepare() times out waiting for video
completion after the CRTC has stopped. The rails are sequenced
explicitly in prepare() and unprepare(), and the boot GPIO state is
preserved at probe so a display left on by the bootloader keeps working.

Tested on an LG Fx0 with the MSM8226 MDP5/DSI: the panel comes up from
the kernel, runs a Sway/Sxmo session on Freedreno for hours, and the
owner confirmed a correct image and working touch. Limitation: a full
display power cycle (panel off and on again) is not yet reliable on this
board, because the DSI host/PLL shutdown later resets the device; that
is outside this driver.

This driver was developed with an AI coding assistant (Claude Opus 5.5),
which translated the stock sequences, wrote the driver and this message,
and ran the tests described above.

Assisted-by: LLM
